{"notebook":"nb1","page":2,"seed":2,"says":"You are right that I measured and then flinched. Fine: it is not yet dawn at this window, and darkness is the one subject where your advice and mine agree, because a night sky honestly is mostly graphite. I will cross-hatch the upper panes hard, let the sky thin toward the horizon, block the rooftops in solid, and then take the eraser to it for two lit kitchens and the moon. Then I sharpen, because words need a point. I am not pressing at 1.4 everywhere, only where it is dark. The point can go blunt on the sky; that is what the sky is for.","before":{"length":174.45424951398033,"worn":0.06647849457885188,"eraser":12,"sharpenings":0,"graphite":0.0559562985485341,"distance":3382.235408766473},"after":{"length":169.65105525188673,"worn":0.05320405916709766,"eraser":11.980383005217794,"sharpenings":1,"graphite":3.375738222613676,"distance":51694.89419122923},"stats":{"strokeM":48.31265878246618,"graphite":3.319781924065146,"used":4.803194262093598,"sharpenings":1,"erasedMm2":74,"coverage":0.15118769246697947,"stopped":false},"warnings":[],"ops":[{"op":"write","text":"6:40. The window before the sun.","x":14,"y":22,"size":7},{"op":"rect","x":18,"y":30,"w":112,"h":120,"pressure":1.2,"repeat":2},{"op":"rect","x":22,"y":34,"w":104,"h":112,"pressure":1},{"op":"rect","x":22,"y":34,"w":50.5,"h":54.5},{"op":"hatch","region":{"rect":[22,34,50.5,54.5]},"angle":35,"spacing":0.5,"cross":true,"pressure":1.4},{"op":"rect","x":22,"y":91.5,"w":50.5,"h":54.5},{"op":"hatch","region":{"rect":[22,91.5,50.5,12]},"angle":35,"spacing":0.6,"cross":true,"pressure":1.2},{"op":"hatch","region":{"rect":[22,103.5,50.5,10]},"angle":35,"spacing":0.9,"cross":true,"pressure":0.9},{"op":"hatch","region":{"rect":[22,113.5,50.5,32.5]},"angle":35,"spacing":1.6,"pressure":0.6},{"op":"hatch","region":{"polygon":[[22,146],[22,128],[30,120],[38,128],[38,124],[52,124],[52,116],[56,116],[56,124],[66,124],[66,130],[72.5,130],[72.5,118],[72.5,130],[72.5,130],[72.5,112],[